      "id": "05653bcd8b0ea5b0e3a3b2f678d32b4398b7183d",
      "message": "[ota-hal] OTA-1681: the outpost lets go\n\nTask #191 \u2014 three outpost notations from the owner's 09-04 log, one root\nbetween two of them.\n\n  19:37  he tapped ENTER OUTPOST at Giant-Watch Shrine with a course plotted\n         to the Mud Seas, walked into Tomb Vigil's entry room, and the travel\n         row showed \"\u2192 MUD SEAS \u00b7 STOP TRAVEL\" instead of the rooms and EXIT:\n         \"I can only go to the very first room and then my only other options\n         are go back to my auto route.\"\n  19:39  he tapped \u2192 MUD SEAS from inside, walked east through open silt, and\n         the minimap kept drawing the outpost: \"my mini-map still shows me\n         stuck in the outpost even though I'm not.\" Still true at 22:05.\n\nROOT. Since OTA-1669 the gate opens with a course still plotted, and two\nthings had never learned that. InputBox let the travel-row branch win over\nthe room row whenever a course existed. And continueTravel never dropped\n`hubRoomId` on the way out \u2014 beginScene only drops it when the LOCATION\nchanges, and a step inside the same location's grid never does, so the room\nrode along under open sky and the minimap drew it faithfully. OTA-993 put \"a\ncourse begins outside\" at setTravelCourse and OTA-1595 at the whisper course;\ncontinueTravel is the third door, and it now carries the same clear and the\nsame line (\"You step out under open sky and take your bearings.\").\n\nHis design, made real: landing never auto-enters (1606); ENTER gives the\nwhole outpost \u2014 rooms + EXIT \u2014 whatever course is plotted; EXIT puts you back\non the tile with the course intact, and the travel row returns.\n\nThe 17:42 notation (ENTER OUTPOST at Tartarian Pilgrim Camp stepping into\nnothing, six taps) was on OTA-1668 and is exactly what OTA-1669 fixed that\nevening; the suite pins that the chip and the gate decide on one predicate so\nit cannot recur as a disagreement.\n\n- app/state/gameStore.ts \u2014 continueTravel: the choke-point clear + line.\n- app/components/InputBox.tsx \u2014 the travel-row branch yields to the room row\n  when inside (`travelTargetName && !hubRoom`).\n- __tests__/ota1681TheOutpostLetsGo.test.ts \u2014 7 tests: the gate opens with a\n  course and the course survives; continuing from inside drops the room, says\n  so, and keeps walking the course; a building interior lets go the same way;\n  outside stays silent; the three doors share one rule; the row order; the one\n  predicate.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LGFtzR6AQJbu4XdR28y3fX",
      "dateCreated": "2026-09-05T03:21:55Z",
